de-xr: See README.XR.md for the original-editor FLTK 1.4.5 / QSV / SBS extension.

Current de-xr build
------------------
The maintained fork uses the original multitrack editor with DomeD's patched
FLTK 1.4.5, native menus, Intel QSV decoding/encoding and per-clip/project SBS
settings. README.XR.md documents the current CMake release build, private legacy
libraries, system/user installation, stereo workflow and hardware limits.

Run openmovieeditor [project.vproj] for the editor, or openmovieeditor --help
for render, project round-trip and subtitle/SMIL export commands. The source
manual is doc/man/openmovieeditor.1; read it with:

    man -l doc/man/openmovieeditor.1

The following upstream notes describe the historical dependency/build setup;
use README.XR.md for this fork's current build instead.

The Open Movie Editor


... is a Non Linear Movie Editor, it is in its very early stages of development.

http://openmovieeditor.sourceforge.net/

-Richard Spindler <richard.spindler AT gmail.com>


Deps:

fltk
libquicktime
gavl (gmerlin audio video library)
libsndfile
ffmpeg (optional but recommended)
jack audio connection kit
libmpeg3
libsamplerate
portaudio (v19)

Installation Hints for Dependencies:

ffmpeg:
 be sure to set at least the following switches at ./configure time:
 ./configure --enable-gpl --enable-shared
 Also check the messages, and make sure that all the codecs that need other
 dependencies are included, and if neccessary enable the appropriate switches
 mentioned in ./configure --help

libquicktime:
 When compiling libquicktime from source make sure that all the fancy codecs are
 enabled in the ./configure script. If some are missing, be sure to install the
 required dependency.

libsndfile:
 There is a yet to be merged variant of libsndfile that supports ogg files. Its
 at http://www.metadecks.org/software/libsndfile/ . However, I do not use it
 because ffmpeg does ogg as well.


